# snapshot-section-schema's starts of core/scripts/validate-artifact-budget.sh (BL-879 grammar). Every other drive is in
# process: run.sh asks vab_main through vab_ip. One cli cell per distinct CLI outcome (exit 1, exit 0), each started as
# FXCELL=<id> bash in vab_eqv() and compared byte for byte with the in-process call on the same input.
cli core/scripts/validate-artifact-budget.sh cli-vab-fail
cli core/scripts/validate-artifact-budget.sh cli-vab-pass
# The verdict.sh arm runs the real verdict renderer, which starts the validator as its own child (its FXCELL tag is inherited).
e2e core/scripts/validate-artifact-budget.sh e2e-verdict-render why=verdict.sh starts the validator as a program (bash "$target") to render the budget summary line, and that start is the mechanism the arm drives
